   "he": "מִי שֶׁהוּטַּל עָלָיו יָדוֹ עַל הָעֶלְיוֹנָה וְכוּ׳. מַנִּי מַתְנִיתִין? לָא רַבִּי נָתָן וְלָא רַבִּי יְהוּדָה הַנָּשִׂיא.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «The one upon whom» the exploitation «was imposed has the advantage.» If he wishes, he can say to the other: Give me back my money and nullify the transaction, or he can say: Give me back the sum that you gained by exploiting me. The Gemara asks: «Whose» opinion is expressed in «the mishna?» It is «neither» the opinion of «Rabbi Natan nor» the opinion of «Rabbi Yehuda HaNasi.»"
  }
